{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:2604bdf2475e5d60238d4b880f670a7a7ebad47d9ca1b7c67a51ffe6346734cc","title":"How should one ask what observers could have measured if a now-known quantity had been unknown? The paper requires a physical specification of which records may vary and which features continue to identify the conditioning system.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2669db91d23e9036f10fb42190e3939f0ae4fa28b56e2142f606a1f3eccad59b","title":"Can a square-root electromagnetic Lagrangian coupled to general relativity, without the standard Maxwell term, produce a linear confining potential? The paper examines magnetic charge and purely electric Nariai–Bertotti–Robinson-type backgrounds through radial charged-particle motion.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:26b28327dd0e24d47c01e4853aa0cac164ac323c0e38bcccddbaf06e78cccc91","title":"Can singular fluxes near anti-branes be interpreted as the stationary description of an instability, resolved by time-dependent flux attraction followed by brane-flux annihilation? The intended application is anti-D3 metastability in the Klebanov–Strassler throat.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:26cac0bab264bed2840cc106cf8fe9a8288356d8f7cc7b397df850f091db8e8d","title":"Can anthropic selection be obtained through conditioning in quantum cosmology, and can the no-boundary quantum state provide a prior that restores an order-of-magnitude prediction for Λ when the primordial fluctuation amplitude Q also scans?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2674f97bb6735f1edb7f47b93d7fb1623efc998bbf2b6adba0f1f689fde9f1be","title":"What scalar-tilt, tensor and spectator-isocurvature predictions does gauged M-flation make in its outer and hilltop inflationary regions, when scanned against the Planck constraints and conditional BICEP2 interpretation available to the authors in 2014?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:264f87d373c365352833583441041998040f9980e5229f50b6e1f47def2b7c3a","title":"Can unitary CFT sequences with large central charge, sparse low-spin spectra and a parametrically large higher-spin gap lack supersymmetry? Such sequences would describe weakly coupled AdS gravity with an Einstein limit.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:260a273e4146d00c705baa5c176b9ba1ac6a1e7d2846526888d550c4b8d10d57","title":"Can a spectator axion–non-Abelian gauge sector in type IIB compactifications produce observable chiral primordial gravitational waves during small-field inflation while preserving moduli stabilization and host inflationary dynamics?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:26ea6818f7ce05e2e20dd0077fc343589292de168548b050ac2802f7fc2efe89","title":"Can strong chiral gauge dynamics in a D-brane axion EFT generate a natural-like inflaton potential, with useful heavy-condensate backreaction and controlled field-theory, wormhole, and weak-gravity effects?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:264a8c24464bf40a7811cc6110c134b3670a98fefbe716f818e3a29549406dc8","title":"Can the scalar responsible for steep-potential inflation become subdominant after inflation and later drive accelerated expansion?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0032"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:269b88addfc1185d719c9c63a0c2f6e1c10bcf7267a6d5f921f8a7c95078326a","title":"How special would precise entropy saturation be in familiar asymptotic string limits? The footnote reduces its discussion to a large-volume setting with a KK tower, after mentioning weak coupling and a conjectural mirror description of large complex structure.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:26224d38ad23afd1743a9c1870a8acde9e87e3c62e7c68459497dd129c4d91e4","title":"Does the leading linear tensor–matter vertex determine its mass renormalization without specifying the nonlinear covariant completion?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:26062d8f046cc696fcd7fde243253e03a0c1cbaacbc1b19f3990969ea234ab50","title":"How are spinless modular-bootstrap bounds on the first nonidentity primary related to sphere-packing bounds, and can analytic bootstrap functionals sharpen constraints on the spectrum of AdS3 quantum gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:26ad2db1df603398d983e1485dd51045c8aaf196aa11294832dcd5e8f1dc1967","title":"Can multiple conformal points remain independently tunable in one compact gravitational theory? The orbifold construction supplies 27 local sectors and Coulomb parameters that can all be set to zero independently.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0042"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:266d522ec69c6c2f1a6cda6c15378a814bf28e2fbae633691d1f125ae161b1e8","title":"Do infinite-distance limits with dominant instanton corrections realize the Emergent String Conjecture? The paper tests whether quantum-corrected trajectories yield a unique lightest, asymptotically tensionless weakly coupled string, or instead a